			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-565969">
									

<p>Thanks, y'all. That is one big difference with 688, in that you <em>could</em> (easily) use 292 for personal gain. But, you can't just have something go wrong and then flip it. 292 doesn't start recording till it's flipped, then you've got 60 seconds to rewind before the sand runs out. It'd be better used just before a short, high-risk activity, then if it fails, flip back over and rewind. Also, potentially, precognition, though only for a minute ahead, and through the déjà vu filter. Plus side effects.</p>

